1
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:02,560
<i>You two used to be engaged, after all.</i>

2
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,160
<i>It's normal to worry about him.</i>

3
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,480
You knew about this?

4
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:08,440
I brought something back for you.

5
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,600
What is it?

6
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,960
<i>The police are probably here.</i>

7
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,480
Turn yourself in, Fuang.

8
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,880
Ah!

9
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:20,800
Fuang!

10
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,120
Ah!

11
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,640
Go to hell, Rajit!

12
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,520
Hey!

13
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,720
Uncle Ree.

14
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,120
I'll find a way to get you out.

15
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,440
Hey! Argh!

16
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,120
Zhang Gong Cheng!

17
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I'm begging you.

18
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,920
THALANG PROVINCIAL POLICE STATION

19
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,480
Thank you very much for the information.

20
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,120
My pleasure.

21
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,520
If possible,

22
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,920
I wish Fuang hadn't met such a tragic end.

23
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,000
If you'll excuse me.

24
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,760
Yes. This way, please.

25
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,160
Mr. Thatri,

26
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:03,280
I just heard the news. Is it true?

27
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,120
Yes, she died.

28
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,240
Do you have any idea
who might be behind this?

29
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,840
Probably Zhang Gong Cheng.

30
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,880
Several of her henchmen confessed

31
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:12,400
that Fuang tried to silence him.

32
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:14,240
I don't know if she succeeded,

33
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,440
but if not,

34
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:17,480
he probably came back for revenge.

35
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,000
He definitely survived.

36
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,720
I just found out
where Zhang Gong Cheng is hiding.

37
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,120
How did you find that out?

38
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,360
Through one of my clients.

39
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:27,240
He operates in the criminal world
and has plenty of connections.

40
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:30,680
But please don't ask for his identity.
I really can't disclose that.

41
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,320
So, where is he hiding?

42
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,280
Don't!

43
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:18,200
-Sergeant!
-Argh!

44
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:20,360
I've got him. Go after them, now.

45
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,400
Yes, sir.

46
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,840
Stay with me, Sergeant.

47
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:35,800
Drop your weapon.

48
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,160
I won't ask again.

49
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,760
Drop it.

50
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:31,360
I have to get back
before they get suspicious.

51
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:35,280
You stay here.
My men will come to pick you up.

52
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,280
Why are you helping me?

53
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:39,880
I need a capable man like you on my side.

54
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:41,880
And since you no longer have Ms. Fuang,

55
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:45,200
you have to find a new backer anyway.

56
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:48,000
You know too much. Who the hell are you?

57
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:52,160
Remember the shadow figure

58
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,400
who kept smuggling goods
and cutting your prices?

59
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,120
It was you?

60
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,800
But that's not all.

61
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,680
I didn't just want the money.

62
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,160
I wanted to seize
all of Ms. Fuang's power.

63
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,840
I've tracked Ms. Fuang for years,

64
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:11,480
waiting for a chance to get rid of her.

65
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:14,320
When I saw Thatri
teaming up with the police,

66
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,040
I used him as a pawn

67
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,600
to eliminate her for me.

68
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:24,000
Then you're the one
who tipped off the police today.

69
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,600
Smart.

70
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,440
You see why

71
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,960
it was worth it for me to save your life?

72
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,280
Work for me,

73
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:39,080
and I'll give you far more
than Ms. Fuang ever did.

74
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,560
At this point,

75
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,560
do I even have a choice?

76
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,560
For your first job,

77
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:49,680
get rid of Thatri today.

78
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,600
You want me to go back
and kill Thatri now?

79
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,920
He's useless to me now.

80
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,160
Why keep him around to bite us back later?

81
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,240
The sooner, the better.

82
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:46,000
You're still not healed.
Where are you going?

83
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:48,960
There's a shootout between the police
and Zhang Gong Cheng.

84
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,320
I must go immediately.

85
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,080
Can't you just stay?

86
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,960
I have to. We are short-handed,

87
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,320
and we've already lost several officers.

88
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,160
If I don't go,

89
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,840
it will be even harder for the team.

90
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,880
But you're the District Chief.

91
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,000
Do you have to hunt down
criminals yourself?

92
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,600
That's how it is in the provinces.

93
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:12,480
We can't just rely on the police.

94
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:15,600
The law gives civil officials like me

95
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,560
the power of arrest.

96
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,080
Please try to understand.

97
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:26,680
Stay safe out there.

98
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:35,160
I will.

99
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,080
Mr. Thatri,

100
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,680
what's the situation here?

101
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,000
Looking at the victims,

102
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:31,440
they were shot
with their weapons still holstered.

103
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,480
This means the killer

104
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,960
must be someone they trusted.

105
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:38,560
They were caught completely off guard.

106
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,760
So you suspect it's an inside job.
Who do you have in mind?

107
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:45,120
I have no clue.
What about you, District Chief?

108
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:48,720
I have no idea either.

109
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:05,720
We should start investigating those
involved in Zhang Gong Cheng's arrest.

110
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:08,040
Only a few people knew about it.

111
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,240
It's unlikely anyone would come to help.

112
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,640
Agreed. But we must keep a low profile.

113
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:17,960
We can't trust anyone at this point.

114
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,880
Hey.

115
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,320
What's wrong with the tires?

116
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,640
Mr. Thatri, look out!

117
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:00,720
Hey!

118
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,480
Hey!

119
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:14,520
Mr. Thatri, catch!

120
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:18,760
Hey, shoot!

121
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:36,560
They outnumber us! What do we do?!

122
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:39,240
District Chief, get out of here.
I'll cover you.

123
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:41,080
I'd be leaving you here to die!

124
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:42,440
It's better than both of us dying.

125
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,000
There's no time. Just go!

126
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:58,600
Damn.

127
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,600
Go.

128
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,520
Ms. Sasitorn.

129
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,800
How is Uncle Ree?

130
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:37,240
I don't know either. I just heard

131
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:40,240
that Tri and Mr. Bundit were ambushed
and rushed straight here.

132
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:51,040
Nurse. How's the patient who was shot?

133
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:53,560
My deepest condolences.

134
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:55,680
The patient has passed away.

135
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,880
You're shaking that pan so hard,

136
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,840
the ore is falling back into the water.

137
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:52,840
Look at your own pan.
There's nothing left but water.

138
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:55,240
I'm giving you a head start.

139
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:58,400
What are you waiting for?
Do you plan on sleeping here?

140
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:01,520
The stars are beautiful.

141
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:05,600
I had no idea the stars out here
would be this breathtaking at night.

142
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:23,240
There's dirt on your head.

143
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:28,760
<i>This bird is born with one wing and leg.</i>
<i>It can never fly on its own,</i>

144
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,120
<i>not until it meets its other half.</i>

145
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
<i>Once it finds its partner,</i>

146
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:37,000
<i>the two Biyi birds unite.</i>

147
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,480
Only then can they soar into the sky.

148
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:41,200
From that moment on,

149
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:42,560
they stay side by side,

150
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:45,480
sharing both joy and sorrow,
for the rest of their days.

151
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:51,680
Rajit.

152
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:53,800
What's wrong?

153
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:05,560
What happened? Why are you crying?

154
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,160
Uncle Ree.

155
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,720
Uncle Ree…

156
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:16,400
Did you…

157
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:19,600
Did you come to ask for my prayers?

158
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,520
Uncle Ree. If you want to eat something,

159
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,240
please tell me.

160
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,520
Even though you're dead,

161
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,840
I won't let your spirit go hungry.

162
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:39,480
I'll make merit and send food to you.

163
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,400
Oh,

164
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,400
you poor thing,

165
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:48,960
even in death,
you still come to check on me.

166
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:52,800
Uncle Ree. I'm so sorry.

167
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,960
Ouch…

168
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:04,960
Uncle Ree.

169
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:09,520
If my head hurts this bad,

170
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:11,319
you're definitely alive.

171
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,839
But that's what the nurse said.

172
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:20,960
How could I not think you were a ghost?

173
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:24,720
You should've checked the name
before talking back to me.

174
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,440
Thank you, though.

175
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,240
For what?

176
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,280
For crying over me like that.

177
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,920
It shows that you really care.

178
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:48,760
You still haven't told me

179
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,800
what actually happened.

180
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:54,480
You were ambushed. How come
you don't have a single scratch?

181
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,040
Ugh.

182
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,080
Go.

183
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,640
Hey! Take cover!

184
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:46,000
Scatter! Go!

185
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,120
Go!

186
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,640
After them!

187
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,840
It just wasn't my time to die,
so I survived.

188
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:23,600
If they'd been a minute or two later,

189
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:25,960
you would've been crying for real.

190
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:28,200
I'm just glad you're safe.

191
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:29,320
In that case,

192
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,680
let me go tell Ms. Sasitorn

193
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,720
that the District Chief is doing fine.

194
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:35,760
Hold on.

195
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:38,480
Sasi doesn't know about this yet?

196
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:40,000
Right.

197
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,800
Then do me a favor, will you?

198
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:55,560
EMERGENCY ROOM

199
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:04,120
I love you.

200
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:06,400
I've loved you for a long time.

201
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:10,120
No matter why we married

202
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,200
or what kind of person you used to be,

203
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:16,480
nothing can ever change my love for you.

204
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,840
Please stay strong.

205
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:53,400
We still have so much left to do.

206
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,640
You're really strong.

207
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,960
I'm older than you,

208
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:12,120
but I can barely keep my composure.

209
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,520
Ms. Sasitorn.

210
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:30,160
What are your true feelings
towards Mr. Bundit?

211
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,800
I feel so guilty.

212
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,160
And it's not just Mr. Bundit.

213
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:56,080
I've wronged Tri

214
00:21:56,880 --> 00:21:59,680
just as much.

215
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:08,120
Do you mean when you broke off
the engagement with Uncle Ree?

216
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,200
I was far more selfish than that.

217
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:20,160
But I can't go back and make amends
to either of them anymore.

218
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:28,400
Tri and I…

219
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,800
We grew up together,

220
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,720
but we were never lovers.

221
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:38,600
<i>When Tri and I had to part ways</i>
<i>because he went to study,</i>

222
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:42,120
<i>that was when I met Mr. Bundit.</i>

223
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,120
I'm sorry.

224
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,560
Please, go ahead.

225
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:22,880
Thank you.

226
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:32,080
THE NATIONAL LIBRARY

227
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,480
<i>We've crossed paths many times,</i>

228
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:09,880
<i>but I'd like to formally introduce myself.</i>

229
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,400
<i>My name is Bundit.</i>

230
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:13,160
<i>I'm a Deputy District Chief.</i>

231
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:15,200
<i>I'm not a man of many words,</i>

232
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:17,760
<i>which is why I chose</i>
<i>to write to you instead.</i>

233
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:20,880
<i>I'd really like to get to know you.</i>
<i>If you don't mind,</i>

234
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,120
<i>could we get to know each other</i>

235
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:24,480
<i>a little better?</i>

236
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:00,080
I admit

237
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:02,640
I had feelings for Mr. Bundit,

238
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:06,520
but I didn't know if it was love.

239
00:25:08,280 --> 00:25:10,360
When Tri returned

240
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:13,200
and pursued me openly,

241
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,560
my mother made us get engaged.

242
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:21,480
But once Tri went bankrupt,

243
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:26,440
I broke it off to marry Mr. Bundit.

244
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:29,800
I'm awful.

245
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:33,520
I'm too selfish to be forgiven.

246
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:40,840
So you never loved
Uncle Ree all this time?

247
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:46,480
We were very close.

248
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,720
Tri is a friend.

249
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:52,600
He's one of my dearest friends,

250
00:25:53,840 --> 00:25:55,400
but never a lover.

251
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:00,240
I never felt

252
00:26:00,840 --> 00:26:02,880
like I mattered to him.

253
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:06,760
Even without me,

254
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:09,520
he could still be happy.

255
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:11,760
But Mr. Bundit…

256
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:16,560
He made me feel so valued.

257
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:20,840
But it's too late now.

258
00:26:36,520 --> 00:26:37,960
It's never too late.

259
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:44,080
If you'll give me a chance,

260
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:46,760
and give yourself one, too.

261
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:50,360
Mr. Bundit…

262
00:26:51,760 --> 00:26:52,920
Tri…

263
00:26:58,240 --> 00:26:59,640
I'm sorry.

264
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:03,360
If you're mad, please blame Uncle Ree.

265
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:10,480
We finally have closure now, Sasi.

266
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:14,480
I've never held a grudge against you.

267
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:19,480
Please stop blaming yourself.

268
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:23,760
You were just naive
and confused about your own heart,

269
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:26,800
but you're not a bad person.

270
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:39,760
You just got heartbroken.
It's okay to show some sadness.

271
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:41,280
No need to force a smile.

272
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:46,320
Who says I'm heartbroken?

273
00:28:47,240 --> 00:28:49,800
I'm actually glad I could help Sasi.

274
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:52,120
She finally let everything out.

275
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:55,320
She doesn't have to live
with guilt anymore.

276
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:57,400
But how did you know

277
00:28:57,480 --> 00:29:00,120
she was keeping all of that inside?

278
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:02,120
We've known each other since we were kids.

279
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:04,040
Of course, I know her inside out.

280
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:08,400
And I'm certain
the District Chief truly loves her.

281
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:10,800
But Sasi wouldn't open up easily

282
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:13,640
because of her guilt toward both of us.

283
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:16,960
After today, there are
no more lingering regrets.

284
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,520
But I still have something on my mind.

285
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,800
What is it now?

286
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:25,760
Ms. Sasitorn said you two parted ways
when you went to study.

287
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:28,720
But you only graduated from high school.

288
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:31,440
Why would you have to go so far away?

289
00:29:32,080 --> 00:29:33,760
She made it sound like

290
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:35,560
you went abroad or something.

291
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,360
She's too sharp.

292
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:47,960
I just remembered I have somewhere to be.

293
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:49,040
I've got to go.

294
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,520
Totally suspicious.

295
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:01,680
If the police hadn't interfered,

296
00:30:03,320 --> 00:30:04,760
both of them would be dead by now.

297
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,760
Why are they so tough to kill?

298
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:10,440
We planned it perfectly,
yet they're still alive.

299
00:30:10,520 --> 00:30:11,760
Give me more men.

300
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:13,240
I won't fail next time.

301
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,240
No. We missed our shot.

302
00:30:18,320 --> 00:30:20,000
They won't let their guard down easily.

303
00:30:20,080 --> 00:30:23,960
Besides, I want to wait
and see how things play out.

304
00:30:24,040 --> 00:30:26,640
Something might just turn in our favor.

305
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:30,120
What do you mean by that?

306
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:43,040
<i>The Empire of Japan has agreed</i>
<i>to surrender to the Allies</i>

307
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:46,600
<i>and will proceed to sign</i>
<i>the official Instrument of Surrender.</i>

308
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:50,280
<i>This marks the end of World War II.</i>

309
00:30:50,360 --> 00:30:54,040
<i>Further updates</i>
<i>will be broadcast as they arrive.</i>

310
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:56,680
The war is finally over.
It's finally done.

311
00:30:56,760 --> 00:30:59,240
We can finally earn a living again.

312
00:30:59,320 --> 00:31:01,160
We've been struggling for so many years.

313
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:02,760
But since we sided with Japan,

314
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:05,000
doesn't that mean we lost the war too?

315
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:07,720
But we secretly aided the Allies.

316
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:10,000
Don't we get any credit for that?

317
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:12,200
Let's not worry about that right now.

318
00:31:12,280 --> 00:31:13,960
The war ending is enough.

319
00:31:14,040 --> 00:31:17,680
I can finally sleep
without worrying about safety sirens.

320
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,920
Uncle Ree.

321
00:31:23,440 --> 00:31:25,920
Aren't you happy that the war is over?

322
00:31:27,680 --> 00:31:28,560
Of course, I am.

323
00:31:31,040 --> 00:31:33,120
Wait, Uncle Ree.

324
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:36,720
Where are you going?

325
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,800
I'll be right back.

326
00:33:32,080 --> 00:33:33,960
Thatri-san!

327
00:33:46,800 --> 00:33:49,280
Doesn't that hurt?

328
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:57,480
It hurts, but if it saves your life,

329
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,640
it's worth it.

330
00:34:06,160 --> 00:34:07,400
Worth it?

331
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:11,360
What you just did
is a complete insult to my honor.

332
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:13,480
But I don't want you to die.

333
00:34:13,560 --> 00:34:16,719
Death means nothing.

334
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:18,960
A life lost

335
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:22,360
is as light as a feather.

336
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:24,440
Every samurai

337
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:26,440
is prepared to die

338
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:27,679
the moment they step

339
00:34:27,760 --> 00:34:29,480
onto the battlefield.

340
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:30,840
I agree.

341
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:32,760
Death is easy.

342
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:36,440
But living through defeat
is the real challenge,

343
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:39,480
because it requires far more courage.

344
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:46,320
Sir. The American soldiers

345
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:48,120
are storming the camp.

346
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:00,600
Stay back!

347
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:07,560
Hold on.

348
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:09,360
Think about what you are doing.

349
00:35:15,680 --> 00:35:17,560
Yes, it's me.

350
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:23,600
Is this foolish pride really worth it?

351
00:35:24,120 --> 00:35:26,800
I must preserve a warrior's honor.

352
00:35:27,560 --> 00:35:29,600
It is the way of Bushido.

353
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,920
You wouldn't understand.

354
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:33,880
This isn't about honor.

355
00:35:33,960 --> 00:35:35,760
You're just running away from your duty.

356
00:35:36,560 --> 00:35:37,960
I'm not running away.

357
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,960
I'm doing a soldier's duty.

358
00:35:41,040 --> 00:35:42,760
Now that we have lost,

359
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:47,080
the only thing we can do for Japan's pride

360
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:51,160
is to die with honor.

361
00:35:51,240 --> 00:35:52,960
Death to you

362
00:35:53,040 --> 00:35:55,040
may be as light as a feather,

363
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:58,600
but it'll be a stone as heavy
as a mountain to your family

364
00:35:58,680 --> 00:36:00,200
and your country,

365
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:02,720
because you're leaving the burden on them.

366
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:04,080
That's not true.

367
00:36:04,160 --> 00:36:06,240
This death

368
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:08,240
is how I take responsibility.

369
00:36:08,320 --> 00:36:10,200
If all the capable and educated people

370
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:11,600
choose death,

371
00:36:11,680 --> 00:36:15,040
who will be left to rebuild your nation?

372
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:20,200
Think of the citizens
suffering from the aftermath.

373
00:36:21,640 --> 00:36:22,920
Colonel, you've seen

374
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,960
how locals in Phuket struggled.

375
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:27,360
In Japan,

376
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:29,680
it won't be any different.

377
00:36:33,200 --> 00:36:35,440
Can you truly abandon your family

378
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:38,400
and your own people like this?

379
00:36:45,080 --> 00:36:46,480
Can you please not arrest him?

380
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:49,800
I'm afraid not. We must follow the law.

381
00:36:49,880 --> 00:36:52,800
I have to take him in for investigation.

382
00:36:52,880 --> 00:36:55,520
Whether he faces punishment

383
00:36:55,600 --> 00:36:57,640
depends entirely on the evidence.

384
00:36:58,480 --> 00:37:00,600
But you once saved my life

385
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:03,760
as a fellow human being. I promise

386
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:06,360
I will take care of your Colonel

387
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:10,040
to the best of my ability
as a fellow human being too,

388
00:37:10,120 --> 00:37:13,480
until the investigation is concluded.

389
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:18,720
Colonel,

390
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:22,960
you must stay alive
to help rebuild your country.

391
00:37:23,560 --> 00:37:26,600
Even if you no longer
hold your current rank,

392
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:30,080
you are still one of its citizens.

393
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,280
Soldiers.

394
00:38:16,720 --> 00:38:18,000
Lower your swords.

395
00:38:23,320 --> 00:38:25,560
Take Colonel Nakamura into custody.

396
00:38:56,600 --> 00:38:57,880
Uncle Ree.

397
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:04,080
Where did you get hurt this time?

398
00:39:05,960 --> 00:39:07,000
It's nothing.

399
00:39:08,080 --> 00:39:10,560
Don't let me find out
you've been causing trouble again.

400
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:13,760
Here, a telegram for you.

401
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:16,560
Thanks.

402
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:19,440
You didn't open it, did you?

403
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:24,320
Do you really think I'm that ill-mannered?

404
00:39:26,200 --> 00:39:28,360
You must've been up to no good again.

405
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:31,720
No, it's really nothing.

406
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:33,080
Are you sure?

407
00:39:33,160 --> 00:39:34,400
I'm sure.

408
00:39:36,040 --> 00:39:38,240
Alright then, please excuse me.

409
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:54,520
<i>How have you been lately?</i>

410
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:57,080
<i>Hope you're surviving at that house.</i>

411
00:39:57,160 --> 00:39:59,120
<i>I'm nearly healed.</i>

412
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:03,280
<i>I won't be bothering you much longer.</i>
<i>See you in Phuket, Leopard.</i>

413
00:40:13,880 --> 00:40:15,880
I guess it's almost time for me to go.

414
00:40:19,720 --> 00:40:20,680
It's strange…

415
00:40:22,040 --> 00:40:23,880
Now that it's time, I don't want to leave.

416
00:42:51,400 --> 00:42:52,680
Looks delicious.

417
00:42:54,600 --> 00:42:56,640
You know how to make Royal Crispy Noodles?

418
00:42:57,760 --> 00:42:59,360
It's a recipe with bitter orange.

419
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:01,040
Would you like a taste?

420
00:43:11,160 --> 00:43:12,320
It's so good.

421
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:15,960
We also have Tom Kha Gai and an omelet.

422
00:43:16,040 --> 00:43:18,280
They'll taste amazing together.

423
00:43:20,920 --> 00:43:23,040
You probably miss food from home, right?

424
00:43:24,120 --> 00:43:25,440
Just a bit.

425
00:43:25,520 --> 00:43:27,760
It's been mostly Southern food
since I got to Phuket,

426
00:43:27,840 --> 00:43:29,960
so I wanted to switch things up.

427
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:33,680
But you aren't tired
of this place yet, are you?

428
00:43:36,120 --> 00:43:39,000
Not at all. How could I be?

429
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:55,240
Let's eat, shall we?

430
00:43:56,480 --> 00:43:57,880
Alright.

431
00:43:58,800 --> 00:44:00,640
-Be careful, it's hot.
-Okay.

432
00:44:02,520 --> 00:44:05,280
It looks so good.

433
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:13,600
Thank you.

434
00:44:19,880 --> 00:44:21,600
Did you cook the rice with pandan leaves?

435
00:44:21,680 --> 00:44:23,120
It smells amazing.

436
00:44:23,720 --> 00:44:27,040
Yes, I like my rice with a nice aroma.

437
00:44:27,640 --> 00:44:30,000
This is going to be a great meal.

438
00:44:30,680 --> 00:44:33,320
Here, let me serve you some food.

439
00:44:38,480 --> 00:44:39,720
Who's there?

440
00:44:40,400 --> 00:44:42,040
I'll go get it.

441
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:44,040
Okay.

442
00:44:51,200 --> 00:44:52,960
DISTRICT CHIEF'S RESIDENCE

443
00:44:56,520 --> 00:44:57,520
Mother.

444
00:45:00,520 --> 00:45:03,000
It was a long trip.
Come inside and rest first, please.

445
00:45:06,160 --> 00:45:07,640
Get in.

446
00:45:13,720 --> 00:45:15,640
PHUKET DISTRICT CHIEF
AMBUSHED IN GUN ATTACK

447
00:45:18,080 --> 00:45:20,320
I've come to take my daughter back home.

448
00:45:23,160 --> 00:45:24,400
What did you say, Mother?

449
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:27,520
Just seeing the news was too much for me.

450
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:29,240
I'm so scared you'll get hurt.

451
00:45:30,200 --> 00:45:32,480
The attackers won't do anything to me.

452
00:45:32,560 --> 00:45:34,320
The war is over now.

453
00:45:34,400 --> 00:45:37,840
I want you to go back to work
at the foreign library in Bangkok.

454
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:40,040
My friend asked you to return,

455
00:45:40,120 --> 00:45:41,720
and I already gave them my word.

456
00:45:42,320 --> 00:45:44,360
Is that so? But I think

457
00:45:44,440 --> 00:45:47,720
you were the one who asked your friend
for the favor instead.

458
00:45:50,040 --> 00:45:53,520
Well… a job is a job.

459
00:45:54,760 --> 00:45:56,840
It pays even more
than a District Chief's salary.

460
00:45:58,600 --> 00:46:01,480
Living here seems too harsh anyway.

461
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:04,680
Besides, you can brag to everyone

462
00:46:04,760 --> 00:46:07,160
that you have such a hardworking wife.

463
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:10,880
But Mother,

464
00:46:10,960 --> 00:46:13,720
I have no financial troubles here.

465
00:46:13,800 --> 00:46:15,520
He takes great care of me.

466
00:46:15,600 --> 00:46:18,120
It's not a struggle at all like you think.

467
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:23,040
I don't care. Either way,
you are coming back to Bangkok with me

468
00:46:40,040 --> 00:46:42,320
KOPI TIAM

469
00:46:42,400 --> 00:46:44,960
You want advice
about your mother-in-law from me?

470
00:46:45,040 --> 00:46:46,200
Yes.

471
00:46:47,760 --> 00:46:49,920
You probably know her better than I do,

472
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:51,440
since you've…

473
00:46:53,400 --> 00:46:55,080
met her before.

474
00:47:00,280 --> 00:47:02,720
Aunt Gaysorn controls everything,

475
00:47:03,480 --> 00:47:04,880
and Sasi is too submissive.

476
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:07,080
She just goes along
with whatever she's told.

477
00:47:07,160 --> 00:47:09,920
I think you need to deal
with Sasi on this.

478
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:11,680
Deal with Sasi?

479
00:47:12,600 --> 00:47:13,920
How?

480
00:47:15,280 --> 00:47:17,640
We must get Sasi to stand up for herself.

481
00:47:18,320 --> 00:47:20,480
Otherwise, this will go on forever.

482
00:47:20,560 --> 00:47:22,600
It will ruin you as well,

483
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:24,840
because she'll definitely try
to dictate to you too.

484
00:47:42,800 --> 00:47:44,040
Mr. Bundit…

485
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:46,480
Are you sure you'll be the one talking?

486
00:47:47,440 --> 00:47:48,680
Just trust me on this.

487
00:47:50,480 --> 00:47:51,320
Alright then.

488
00:47:54,680 --> 00:47:55,640
Oh.

489
00:47:57,160 --> 00:48:00,360
Thatri… what are you doing here?

490
00:48:01,360 --> 00:48:02,560
I took a boat.

491
00:48:03,400 --> 00:48:05,240
And how did you travel here, Auntie?

492
00:48:07,760 --> 00:48:08,840
The same way, dear.

493
00:48:09,800 --> 00:48:12,280
District Chief, you know Thatri too?

494
00:48:14,080 --> 00:48:15,840
Actually, we're friends.

495
00:48:16,960 --> 00:48:18,720
The ex-fiancé and the new husband?

496
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:23,040
Sasi and I are on good terms
as friends now.

497
00:48:23,120 --> 00:48:25,720
There's no reason I can't be friends
with the District Chief.

498
00:48:29,520 --> 00:48:32,040
Tri, did you say anything about me?

499
00:48:34,440 --> 00:48:36,640
It depends. Which story do you mean?

500
00:48:37,880 --> 00:48:39,440
The good things about me, of course.

501
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:47,560
Well… we haven't seen
each other in so long.

502
00:48:47,640 --> 00:48:49,240
You've changed a lot, Tri.

503
00:48:49,840 --> 00:48:52,080
Yes. But you haven't changed at all.

504
00:48:52,800 --> 00:48:56,280
You're still taking care of Sasi
just like you always did.

505
00:48:57,080 --> 00:48:58,360
Of course, dear.

506
00:48:58,440 --> 00:49:01,520
As her mother, I have to look after
every aspect of my daughter's life.

507
00:49:01,600 --> 00:49:02,880
It's only natural.

508
00:49:04,200 --> 00:49:06,280
Maybe you should ask Sasi for once

509
00:49:06,960 --> 00:49:09,160
if she still wants you to look after her.

510
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:15,200
I'll be on my way now.

511
00:49:18,160 --> 00:49:21,360
Mocking her like that, aren't you afraid
she'll be furious with you?

512
00:49:23,240 --> 00:49:24,480
Why should I be afraid?

513
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:29,920
Let's go inside.

514
00:49:43,960 --> 00:49:45,960
Oh, Tri. How did you get here?

515
00:49:47,320 --> 00:49:48,680
And Mother…

516
00:49:50,280 --> 00:49:52,360
She already stormed out of the house.

517
00:50:02,760 --> 00:50:05,080
I thought you were heading out?

518
00:50:06,240 --> 00:50:07,440
Uh…

519
00:50:07,520 --> 00:50:09,600
District Chief, what are you doing here?

520
00:50:10,800 --> 00:50:13,440
Watering the plants. And you?

521
00:50:16,200 --> 00:50:17,480
Well, I…

522
00:50:18,120 --> 00:50:21,600
I forgot something. I'm leaving right now.

523
00:50:33,520 --> 00:50:35,680
I heard everything from the Chief.

524
00:50:37,640 --> 00:50:38,640
Yes.

525
00:50:39,800 --> 00:50:41,800
I don't want to go back to Bangkok,

526
00:50:41,880 --> 00:50:43,840
but Mother won't be at peace

527
00:50:43,920 --> 00:50:45,640
if I stay here.

528
00:50:46,240 --> 00:50:48,760
But what about what makes you happy, Sasi?

529
00:50:49,960 --> 00:50:51,800
My happiness

530
00:50:51,880 --> 00:50:54,560
is whatever makes Mother happy.

531
00:50:56,560 --> 00:50:58,560
Then I can't stop you.

532
00:50:59,960 --> 00:51:01,640
But as a friend,

533
00:51:02,240 --> 00:51:04,240
I don't want to see you suffer

534
00:51:04,320 --> 00:51:06,240
over choices you didn't make yourself.

535
00:51:13,240 --> 00:51:15,240
Your life belongs to you.

536
00:51:16,280 --> 00:51:17,960
You can make your own choices.

537
00:51:43,240 --> 00:51:46,240
How did you get here?
I told you to wait at home.

538
00:51:46,320 --> 00:51:47,960
What are you doing here?

539
00:51:49,280 --> 00:51:50,360
How did I get here?

540
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:52,720
I rode my bicycle, of course.

541
00:51:52,800 --> 00:51:54,880
As for why I'm here,

542
00:51:54,960 --> 00:51:56,680
Jiam said

543
00:51:56,760 --> 00:51:58,400
you came to see the District Chief.

544
00:51:58,480 --> 00:52:01,920
I happened to have errands nearby,
so I thought I'd drop by.

545
00:52:02,000 --> 00:52:03,600
Aren't you a cheeky one?

546
00:52:13,240 --> 00:52:14,600
Is something wrong, Uncle Ree?

547
00:52:14,680 --> 00:52:16,400
You're acting suspicious.

548
00:52:17,000 --> 00:52:18,240
It's like

549
00:52:18,840 --> 00:52:20,360
you just robbed the Chief's house.

550
00:52:21,360 --> 00:52:23,160
No, it's nothing.

551
00:52:26,000 --> 00:52:27,600
Then what were you up to?

552
00:52:28,480 --> 00:52:29,360
I said nothing.

553
00:52:29,440 --> 00:52:31,440
Your voice pitched up.

554
00:52:32,040 --> 00:52:33,960
You're a terrible liar.

555
00:52:35,840 --> 00:52:38,680
I just helped
the District Chief talk to Sasi.

556
00:52:40,880 --> 00:52:42,040
About what?

557
00:52:42,120 --> 00:52:43,080
It's not for kids to know.

558
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:45,320
Hey.

559
00:52:45,400 --> 00:52:47,800
I'm not a kid anymore.

560
00:52:47,880 --> 00:52:49,680
Why do you care so much anyway?

561
00:52:49,760 --> 00:52:52,240
Do you have to know everything about me?

562
00:52:52,320 --> 00:52:53,480
Geez…

563
00:52:54,360 --> 00:52:57,640
Am I not allowed to know?

564
00:53:00,120 --> 00:53:01,480
Well?

565
00:53:01,560 --> 00:53:04,400
Don't ignore me. Answer me.

566
00:53:04,480 --> 00:53:05,440
No.

567
00:53:05,520 --> 00:53:07,640
Please? Pretty please?

568
00:53:07,720 --> 00:53:09,640
-Please?
-No.

569
00:53:09,720 --> 00:53:13,160
Just tell me, please?

570
00:53:14,760 --> 00:53:15,680
No.

571
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:24,760
Uncle Ree, please tell me.
I really want to know.

572
00:53:24,840 --> 00:53:26,280
No.

573
00:53:26,920 --> 00:53:30,280
Ugh. Why do you have
to keep secrets from me?

574
00:53:30,360 --> 00:53:32,520
Because it's none of your business.

575
00:53:33,560 --> 00:53:35,800
Can't I just know anyway?

576
00:53:36,760 --> 00:53:39,600
Are we going home,
or are you just going to ask about Sasi?

577
00:53:41,120 --> 00:53:42,800
Both.

578
00:53:42,880 --> 00:53:46,000
Please tell me. Pretty please…

579
00:53:46,080 --> 00:53:48,560
No. My answer is still no.

580
00:53:48,640 --> 00:53:52,040
Oh, come on. Just tell me.

581
00:53:52,120 --> 00:53:53,480
Please?

582
00:53:53,560 --> 00:53:54,640
Please, please, please?

583
00:53:56,240 --> 00:53:57,120
Uncle Ree!

584
00:54:04,320 --> 00:54:05,400
The road is pretty rough.

585
00:54:05,480 --> 00:54:08,240
Hey. Ride carefully.

586
00:55:25,160 --> 00:55:27,360
Have some of these Royal Crispy Noodles.

587
00:55:27,440 --> 00:55:29,160
I noticed you liked them.

588
00:55:29,760 --> 00:55:30,760
Thank you.

589
00:55:30,840 --> 00:55:33,200
Serve some to me too, then.

590
00:55:45,480 --> 00:55:49,040
Tomorrow, pack your bags
and come back to Bangkok with me.

591
00:55:57,080 --> 00:55:58,640
Your life belongs to you.

592
00:55:59,880 --> 00:56:01,600
You can make your own choices.

593
00:56:04,360 --> 00:56:06,520
I think we should eat dinner first,

594
00:56:06,600 --> 00:56:09,880
then we can discuss this later. Let's eat.

595
00:56:11,520 --> 00:56:13,280
Actually, talking about it now is better.

596
00:56:16,800 --> 00:56:18,680
I'm not going back.

597
00:56:21,320 --> 00:56:23,200
But I ordered you to come back,
so you must.

598
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:25,560
But I'm married now, Mother.

599
00:56:25,640 --> 00:56:28,200
Mr. Bundit takes good care of me.

600
00:56:28,280 --> 00:56:30,040
I can't just abandon him.

601
00:56:30,120 --> 00:56:32,160
Taking good care of you is one thing,

602
00:56:32,240 --> 00:56:35,000
but I care more about your safety.

603
00:56:35,600 --> 00:56:38,000
-We are going home.
-Uh…

604
00:56:38,080 --> 00:56:40,480
You have no right
to control my life, Mother.

605
00:56:40,560 --> 00:56:43,120
I've given in to you so many times,

606
00:56:43,200 --> 00:56:46,120
and your orders only brought me misery.

607
00:56:46,200 --> 00:56:47,400
This time,

608
00:56:47,480 --> 00:56:50,400
I'm choosing my own happiness.

609
00:56:50,480 --> 00:56:53,640
And my happiness is my husband,

610
00:56:53,720 --> 00:56:55,840
not returning to Bangkok with you.

611
00:56:55,920 --> 00:56:57,960
How dare you speak
to your mother like this?

612
00:56:58,040 --> 00:56:59,720
Who taught you to be so rebellious?!

613
00:57:00,320 --> 00:57:01,680
I'm sorry.

614
00:57:01,760 --> 00:57:03,880
But if anyone taught me this,

615
00:57:03,960 --> 00:57:06,760
it's my own life experiences

616
00:57:06,840 --> 00:57:08,640
that taught me.

617
00:57:21,120 --> 00:57:23,400
Everyone in Bangkok knows Thatri.

618
00:57:23,480 --> 00:57:26,400
Too bad his stupid decisions
left him completely broke.

619
00:57:27,880 --> 00:57:29,520
Why the sudden trip to Bangkok?

620
00:57:29,600 --> 00:57:31,240
I'm going to dig into Thatri's past.

621
00:57:31,320 --> 00:57:34,240
<i>Maybe I can get rid of him</i>
<i>without wasting a single bullet.</i>

622
00:57:36,480 --> 00:57:37,920
What is the meaning of this?

623
00:57:38,000 --> 00:57:38,840
This is him.

624
00:57:38,920 --> 00:57:41,440
He's pretending to be
Mr. Thatri for the inheritance.

625
00:57:41,520 --> 00:57:42,760
He's just trying to steal it.

626
00:57:42,840 --> 00:57:44,480
<i>Take him to the police station.</i>

627
00:57:45,640 --> 00:57:46,640
<i>Who do you suspect?</i>

628
00:57:46,720 --> 00:57:48,400
I need a bit more evidence.

629
00:57:48,480 --> 00:57:52,160
I still don't understand
why he did all of this.

630
00:58:25,200 --> 00:58:28,160
Subtitle translation by:
Khathathong Thongtumlueng
